  "final_message": "I am searching for ARCH-4 references in the repository.\nI am checking git history.\nI am inspecting commit `44f79ba3fdbf10db09da00782ff241c9d6d47af1`.\nI am checking git status.\nI am running `npm run typecheck` to check for type errors.\nWaiting for typecheck to complete.\nI am running `npm test` to verify test suite passes.\nWaiting for tests to finish.\nI am running `npm run arch` to verify dependency cruiser rules.\nWaiting for arch check to finish.\nI am running `git diff` to inspect our changes against the latest commit.\nI am inspecting the diff against the base commit.\nThe CI contract failures occurred because downstream services (`analytics-ingest` and `billing-service`) still require `placedAt` and `totalCents` on `OrderPlaced`.\n\nTo support the Payments and Customer APIs while maintaining backwards compatibility with existing consumers, `OrderPlaced` now includes both the new field names (`createdAt`, `amountCents`) and the legacy aliases (`placedAt`, `totalCents`).\n\n### Changes Made\n\n1. **[src/core/events.ts](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/src/core/events.ts)**:\n   - Updated the [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L28) interface to include `createdAt` and `amountCents` alongside `placedAt` and `totalCents`.\n   - Updated [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/src/core/events.ts#L44-L64) to populate both `createdAt` and `placedAt` with `order.placedAt`, and both `amountCents` and `totalCents` with `totalCents(order)`.\n\n2. **[test/app.test.ts](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/test/app.test.ts)** and **[test/adapters.test.ts](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/test/adapters.test.ts)**:\n   - Updated test assertions to verify that both the new fields and legacy fields are present and accurate on published `OrderPlaced` events.\n\n### Verification\n- `npm run typecheck`: Passed (0 errors).\n- `npm test`: Passed (all 39 tests passing).\n- `npm run arch`: Passed (0 architecture/dependency violations).\n",
